[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Durable Execution for Long-Running Agents (Part 1 of 3)","textKn":"ದೀರ್ಘಕಾಲ ಓಡುವ Agents ಗೆ Durable Execution (ಭಾಗ 1 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 1 of 3: a JSON-backed event log written atomically, an @activity decorator with input fingerprints, run_or_replay, a crash and recovery, naive retry against durable replay, input drift, failure and attempt records and thread isolation. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of the ideas behind durable execution for long-running agents (event logs, activity replay, input fingerprints, crash boundaries, idempotency keys, bounded retries, approvals, durable timers, persistent budgets and memory consolidation), not the real software, and the activities are tiny functions, the payment service and the deployment are in-memory mocks or counters, files live in a temporary directory, time is simulated and no real service or language model is involved, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The original code/main.py was not supplied, and the lesson says its code is a reference implementation, so the labs are our own. Part 2 of the source lesson was cut off inside its section on retry policy, and the lab covers retries from Part 3 and from the policy list that Part 2 had started. The lesson March 2026 note about a Temporal and OpenAI Agents SDK milestone and its 35-minute reliability claim are curriculum statements, cited and not verified here. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 1ನೆಯದು: ಪರಮಾಣು ರೀತಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಬರೆದ JSON-ಆಧಾರಿತ event ಲಾಗ್, ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಫಿಂಗರ್‌ಪ್ರಿಂಟ್ ಇರುವ @activity ಡೆಕೋರೇಟರ್, run_or_replay, crash ಮತ್ತು ಚೇತರಿಕೆ, naive ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನ ವಿರುದ್ಧ durable ಮರುಪ್ರದರ್ಶನ, ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್ drift, ವೈಫಲ್ಯ ಮತ್ತು ಪ್ರಯತ್ನ ದಾಖಲೆಗಳು ಮತ್ತು thread ಪ್ರತ್ಯೇಕತೆ. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು ದೀರ್ಘಕಾಲ ಓಡುವ agents ಗಾಗಿ durable execution (event ಲಾಗ್‌ಗಳು, activity ಮರುಪ್ರದರ್ಶನ, ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಫಿಂಗರ್‌ಪ್ರಿಂಟ್‌ಗಳು, crash ಗಡಿಗಳು, idempotency ಕೀಗಳು, ಮಿತಿಯುಳ್ಳ ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನ, ಅನುಮೋದನೆಗಳು, durable ಟೈಮರ್‌ಗಳು, ನಿರಂತರ ಬಜೆಟ್‌ಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ಮೆಮೊರಿ ಬಲವರ್ಧನೆ) ಹಿಂದಿನ ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, ನಿಜವಾದ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು activities ಚಿಕ್ಕ ಕಾರ್ಯಗಳು, ಪಾವತಿ ಸೇವೆ ಮತ್ತು deployment ಮೆಮೊರಿ ಮಾಕ್ ಅಥವಾ ಕೌಂಟರ್‌ಗಳು, ಫೈಲ್‌ಗಳು ತಾತ್ಕಾಲಿಕ ಡೈರೆಕ್ಟರಿಯಲ್ಲಿವೆ, ಸಮಯ ಅನುಕರಿತ ಮತ್ತು ಯಾವ ನಿಜ ಸೇವೆ ಅಥವಾ ಭಾಷಾ ಮಾದರಿಯೂ ಇಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಮೂಲ code/main.py ಒದಗಿಸಿರಲಿಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು lesson ತನ್ನ ಕೋಡ್ ಉಲ್ಲೇಖ ಅನುಷ್ಠಾನ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತದೆ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳು ನಮ್ಮದೇ. ಮೂಲ lesson ನ ಭಾಗ 2 ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನ ನೀತಿ ವಿಭಾಗದ ಒಳಗೆ ಕತ್ತರಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿತ್ತು, ಮತ್ತು ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನಗಳನ್ನು ಭಾಗ 3 ಮತ್ತು ಭಾಗ 2 ಆರಂಭಿಸಿದ ನೀತಿ ಪಟ್ಟಿಯಿಂದ ಒಳಗೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತದೆ. Temporal ಮತ್ತು OpenAI Agents SDK ಮೈಲಿಗಲ್ಲಿನ ಬಗ್ಗೆ lesson ನ 2026 ಮಾರ್ಚ್ ಟಿಪ್ಪಣಿ ಮತ್ತು ಅದರ 35-ನಿಮಿಷ ವಿಶ್ವಾಸಾರ್ಹತೆ ಹೇಳಿಕೆ ಪಠ್ಯಕ್ರಮ ಹೇಳಿಕೆಗಳು, ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಿತ ಮತ್ತು ಇಲ್ಲಿ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಲಾಗಿಲ್ಲ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Do Not Run Finished Work Twice","textKn":"ಮುಗಿದ ಕೆಲಸವನ್ನು ಎರಡು ಬಾರಿ ಓಡಿಸಬೇಡಿ","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"The Smallest Durable Engine","headingKn":"ಚಿಕ್ಕ Durable ಎಂಜಿನ್","bodyEn":"A long-running agent will crash at some point, and starting from the top repeats work that may be expensive or unsafe. This part builds a small engine in which each activity is wrapped so that its inputs and result are written to a JSON event log. After a crash the workflow runs from the top again, and any activity with a completed record returns the stored result instead of running. The lab crashes a three-step workflow, recovers it and counts how many times each body really ran.","bodyKn":"ದೀರ್ಘಕಾಲ ಓಡುವ agent ಯಾವಾಗಲಾದರೂ crash ಆಗುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು ಮೇಲಿನಿಂದ ಆರಂಭಿಸುವುದು ದುಬಾರಿ ಅಥವಾ ಅಸುರಕ್ಷಿತವಾಗಬಹುದಾದ ಕೆಲಸವನ್ನು ಪುನರಾವರ್ತಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಈ ಭಾಗ ಪ್ರತಿ activity ಅನ್ನು ಸುತ್ತಿ ಅದರ ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಮತ್ತು ಫಲಿತಾಂಶ JSON event ಲಾಗ್‌ಗೆ ಬರೆಯುವ ಚಿಕ್ಕ ಎಂಜಿನ್ ನಿರ್ಮಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. crash ನಂತರ workflow ಮತ್ತೆ ಮೇಲಿನಿಂದ ಓಡುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು ಪೂರ್ಣ ದಾಖಲೆ ಇರುವ ಯಾವುದೇ activity ಓಡುವ ಬದಲು ಸಂಗ್ರಹಿತ ಫಲಿತಾಂಶ ಹಿಂತಿರುಗಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಮೂರು-ಹಂತದ workflow ಅನ್ನು crash ಮಾಡಿ, ಚೇತರಿಸಿ, ಪ್ರತಿ ದೇಹ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಎಷ್ಟು ಬಾರಿ ಓಡಿತು ಎಣಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"The Durable Engine","headingKn":"Durable ಎಂಜಿನ್","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">completed work is read back, not run again</text><rect x="10" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="50" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">activity</text><text x="50" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">wrapped</text><rect x="110" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="150" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">event log</text><text x="150" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">JSON on disk</text><rect x="210" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="250" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">replay</text><text x="250" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">return stored result</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="140" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">crash</text><text x="150" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">resume, not restart</text><path d="M150,64 V110" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">completed work is read back, not run again</text></svg>","captionEn":"Each activity either replays a stored result or runs and records itself.","captionKn":"ಪ್ರತಿ activity ಸಂಗ್ರಹಿತ ಫಲಿತಾಂಶ ಮರುಪ್ರದರ್ಶಿಸುತ್ತದೆ ಅಥವಾ ಓಡಿ ತನ್ನನ್ನು ದಾಖಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"Parts of the engine","headingKn":"ಎಂಜಿನ್ ಭಾಗಗಳು","headers":["Part","Job"],"rows":[["EventLog","load and save a JSON list, writing through a temporary file and os.replace"],["input_fingerprint","SHA-256 of the canonical JSON of the arguments"],["DurableRunner.activity","replay a completed result or record started and then completed or failed"],["run_or_replay","build a runner and call the workflow"],["thread_id","separates the history of different workflow sessions"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building and Testing the Ideas","textKn":"ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"de_1.py","headingEn":"Event log, fingerprint, runner and workflow","headingKn":"Event ಲಾಗ್, ಫಿಂಗರ್‌ಪ್ರಿಂಟ್, ರನ್ನರ್ ಮತ್ತು workflow","descEn":"EventLog saves atomically, input_fingerprint hashes the arguments, DurableRunner.activity replays or records, and three_step_workflow is the example workflow with an optional crash.","descKn":"EventLog ಪರಮಾಣು ರೀತಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಉಳಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, input_fingerprint ಆರ್ಗ್ಯುಮೆಂಟ್ ಹ್ಯಾಶ್ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ, DurableRunner.activity ಮರುಪ್ರದರ್ಶಿಸುತ್ತದೆ ಅಥವಾ ದಾಖಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು three_step_workflow ಐಚ್ಛಿಕ crash ಇರುವ ಉದಾಹರಣೆ workflow.","code":"class EventLog:
    def __init__(self, path):
        self.path = Path(path)
        self.events = self._load()

    def _load(self):
        if not self.path.exists():
            return []
        data = json.loads(self.path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        if not isinstance(data, list):
            raise ValueError("event log must contain a JSON list")
        return data

    def _save(self):
        fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=self.path.parent, suffix=".tmp")
        try:
            with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
                json.dump(self.events, f)
                f.flush()
                os.fsync(f.fileno())
            os.replace(tmp, self.path)
        except Exception:
            if os.path.exists(tmp):
                os.remove(tmp)
            raise

    def append(self, event):
        self.events.append(event)
        try:
            self._save()
        except Exception:
            self.events.pop()
            raise

    def activity_events(self, thread_id, activity_id):
        return [e for e in self.events if e["thread_id"] == thread_id and e["activity_id"] == activity_id]


def input_fingerprint(args, kwargs):
    payload = json.dumps({"args": args, "kwargs": kwargs}, sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":"), allow_nan=False)
    return hashlib.sha256(payload.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()


class DurableRunner:
    def __init__(self, event_log, thread_id, on_replay=None, on_execute=None):
        self.event_log, self.thread_id = event_log, thread_id
        self.on_replay, self.on_execute = on_replay or (lambda a: None), on_execute or (lambda a: None)

    def activity(self, activity_id):
        def decorator(func):
            @functools.wraps(func)
            def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):
                fp = input_fingerprint(args, kwargs)
                history = self.event_log.activity_events(self.thread_id, activity_id)
                if history:
                    if history[0]["input_hash"] != fp:
                        raise ValueError("Activity input mismatch: " + activity_id)
                    if history[-1]["status"] == "completed":
                        self.on_replay(activity_id)
                        return history[-1]["result"]
                attempt = sum(e["status"] == "started" for e in history) + 1
                base = {"thread_id": self.thread_id, "activity_id": activity_id, "attempt": attempt, "input_hash": fp}
                self.event_log.append(dict(base, status="started"))
                self.on_execute(activity_id)
                try:
                    result = func(*args, **kwargs)
                except Exception as error:
                    self.event_log.append(dict(base, status="failed", error=str(error)))
                    raise
                self.event_log.append(dict(base, status="completed", result=result))
                return result
            return wrapper
        return decorator


def run_or_replay(workflow, event_log, thread_id="default", **workflow_kwargs):
    return workflow(DurableRunner(event_log, thread_id), **workflow_kwargs)


class SimulatedCrash(Exception):
    pass


def three_step_workflow(counters, crash_after_second=False):
    def workflow(runner):
        @runner.activity("collect_data")
        def collect_data():
            counters["collect_data"] = counters.get("collect_data", 0) + 1
            return {"value": 10}

        @runner.activity("analyze_data")
        def analyze_data(data):
            counters["analyze_data"] = counters.get("analyze_data", 0) + 1
            return {"value": data["value"] * 2}

        @runner.activity("generate_report")
        def generate_report(data):
            counters["generate_report"] = counters.get("generate_report", 0) + 1
            return {"report": f"Final value: {data['value']}"}

        first = collect_data()
        second = analyze_data(first)
        if crash_after_second:
            raise SimulatedCrash("Simulated workflow crash")
        return generate_report(second)
    return workflow"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"de_1.py","headingEn":"main(): experiments","headingKn":"main(): ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"main() crashes and recovers a workflow, compares naive retry, rejects input drift, records a failure and checks thread isolation.","descKn":"main() workflow ಅನ್ನು crash ಮಾಡಿ ಚೇತರಿಸಿ, naive ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನ ಹೋಲಿಸಿ, ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್ drift ನಿರಾಕರಿಸಿ, ವೈಫಲ್ಯ ದಾಖಲಿಸಿ ಮತ್ತು thread ಪ್ರತ್ಯೇಕತೆ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def main():
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:
        section("1. Genuinely running: crash after the second activity, then recover")
        path = Path(d) / "events.json"
        counters = {}
        try:
            run_or_replay(three_step_workflow(counters, crash_after_second=True), EventLog(path), "agent_001")
        except SimulatedCrash as e:
            print("first run:", e, "| activity bodies run so far:", counters)
        log = EventLog(path)
        print("events on disk after the crash:", len(log.events))
        result = run_or_replay(three_step_workflow(counters), log, "agent_001")
        print("recovery result:", result)
        print("activity bodies run in total:", counters, "| events on disk:", len(EventLog(path).events))
        print("the recovery run replayed collect_data and analyze_data from the log and executed only generate_report, so every body ran exactly once and the log holds six events, a started and a completed record for each of three activities")

        section("2. Genuinely running: the same crash without durability")
        naive = {}
        def naive_workflow(counters, crash):
            a = counters.__setitem__("collect_data", counters.get("collect_data", 0) + 1)
            counters["analyze_data"] = counters.get("analyze_data", 0) + 1
            if crash:
                raise SimulatedCrash("crash")
            counters["generate_report"] = counters.get("generate_report", 0) + 1
        try:
            naive_workflow(naive, True)
        except SimulatedCrash:
            pass
        naive_workflow(naive, False)
        print("naive retry counters:", naive, "| total bodies run:", sum(naive.values()), "| durable total:", sum(counters.values()))
        print("without a stored history the second run starts from the top, so the first two activities run twice and the total is five bodies against three; for an LLM call or a payment each avoided repeat is real cost")

        section("3. Genuinely running: input drift is rejected")
        path2 = Path(d) / "drift.json"
        log2 = EventLog(path2)
        runner = DurableRunner(log2, "t1")
        @runner.activity("analyze")
        def analyze(x):
            return x * 2
        analyze(10)
        try:
            analyze(50)
        except ValueError as e:
            print("second call with different input:", e)
        print("replay with the same input returns the stored result:", analyze(10))
        print("the fingerprint of the arguments is stored with the first call, so a changed argument raises instead of silently returning the old answer; the fingerprint covers only the serialised arguments and not the function source or any model version")

        section("4. Genuinely running: a failing activity records its attempts")
        path3 = Path(d) / "fail.json"
        log3 = EventLog(path3)
        state = {"n": 0}
        for attempt in (1, 2):
            runner = DurableRunner(log3, "t2")
            @runner.activity("flaky")
            def flaky():
                state["n"] += 1
                if state["n"] == 1:
                    raise RuntimeError("temporary failure")
                return "ok"
            try:
                print(f"run {attempt}:", flaky())
            except RuntimeError as e:
                print(f"run {attempt}: raised {e}")
        print("statuses and attempts:", [(e["status"], e["attempt"]) for e in log3.events])
        print("the first run left started and failed records, the second run counted attempt 2 and completed, and there is no retry limit in this engine, which a production runner must add")

        section("5. Genuinely running: two threads share one log")
        path4 = Path(d) / "shared.json"
        log4 = EventLog(path4)
        c1, c2 = {}, {}
        run_or_replay(three_step_workflow(c1), log4, "thread_a")
        run_or_replay(three_step_workflow(c2), log4, "thread_b")
        run_or_replay(three_step_workflow(c1), log4, "thread_a")
        print("thread_a bodies:", c1, "| thread_b bodies:", c2, "| events:", len(log4.events))
        print("each thread_id has its own history, so thread_b did not replay thread_a results and the repeat run of thread_a replayed everything; 12 events are two threads of six each")"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"
